é no pueden demostrar: El hecho de que se adjudiquen contratos justo por debajo del límite no prueba que haya sido un error o que se haya actuado mal. Puede ser una decisión basada en precios de mercado o necesidades específicas.\nQué se puede revisar: Es importante comprobar si los contratos [1], [2] y [3] atienden la misma necesidad. También revisar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas distintas o si hubo ajustes en el presupuesto al final del año.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 35 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 4.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 7.3, with a 95% confidence interval of 4.2 to 12.8. December accounts for 9% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 6% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 3. Contract [1], for 14,910 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not prove improper actions. It could reflect market conditions, budget constraints, or separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate wrongdoing without further investigation.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contracts' dates and awardees to see if multiple contracts serve the same purpose. Review the specific services or goods described in contract [1] to ensure they align with the body's needs. Verify if the same awardee was used for multiple contracts to assess if this was a consistent practice.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["eMsQ3gJrIvuIzo3LHNPGcQ%3D%3D","4eALrVZ3SdZVYjgxA4nMUw%3D%3D","Eo2oQa1nlkYwYTJJ03sHog%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}